---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import GradientText from "../../components/GradientText.astro";
import PlayableNav from "../../components/PlayableNav.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Playable Ads QA & Release Readiness | Aniloom Technologies" description="Risk-based QA and release-readiness review for playable ads across responsive states, interactions, variants, and target platform constraints.">
  <main id="main-content">
    <PlayableNav />
    <section class="page-hero page-hero--service section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Playable Ads / QA & Release Readiness</p>
      <h1 data-reveal>Know what was checked, what remains open, and <GradientText>what happens next.</GradientText></h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lead" data-reveal>We review an existing playable against its intended journey, meaningful states, target orientations, agreed variants, and known platform constraints, then make the evidence and remaining risk usable for a release decision.</p>
      <div class="page-hero__actions" data-reveal><button class="button" type="button" data-contact-open>Discuss a review</button><a class="text-link" href="#review">See what we review <span>↓</span></a></div>
    </section>

    <section class="entry-points section-shell section-pad" id="review">
      <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">Risk-based review</p><h2>Test the experience, not only the file.</h2></div><p>The review starts from the intended campaign action and the failures that would most damage the journey, presentation, integration, or release.</p></div>
      <div class="review-grid">
        <article data-reveal><span>Journey</span><h3>From entry to campaign action</h3><p>Core interaction, progression, feedback, calls to action, end cards, links, replay behavior, and failure or exit paths.</p></article>
        <article data-reveal><span>Presentation</span><h3>Every meaningful state</h3><p>Layout, scale, fonts, visual hierarchy, readability, controls, animation states, and content that appears during the flow.</p></article>
        <article data-reveal><span>Responsive</span><h3>Portrait and landscape</h3><p>Representative viewport sizes, orientation changes, safe areas, cropping, alignment, and interaction reach across agreed states.</p></article>
        <article data-reveal><span>Readiness</span><h3>Variants and platforms</h3><p>Agreed builds, localization or creative variants, integration behavior, target-environment constraints, and known limitations.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="system-band section-pad">
      <div class="section-shell">
        <div class="section-heading" data-reveal><div><p class="eyebrow">The output</p><h2>Evidence for a decision, not a quality claim.</h2></div><p>Aniloom reports what was reviewed, the evidence observed, what could not be checked, and which risks still need an owner.</p></div>
        <div class="deliverable-grid">
          <div data-reveal><span>Risk and coverage view</span><p>Priority flows, meaningful states, target configurations, and explicit gaps or assumptions.</p></div>
          <div data-reveal><span>Actionable issue record</span><p>Reproduction context, observed behavior, expected behavior, supporting evidence, severity, and ownership.</p></div>
          <div data-reveal><span>Correction and retest</span><p>Saved changes or developer corrections, affected states, regression checks, and retest results.</p></div>
          <div data-reveal><span>Release disposition</span><p>A concise view of tested scope, open risks, blocked areas, accepted limitations, and the decision still required.</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="system-note" data-reveal>This work is not certification and does not guarantee defect-free delivery, campaign performance, or acceptance by an advertising platform.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="quality-lead section-pad">
      <div class="section-shell quality-lead__grid">
        <div data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">Quality responsibility</p><h2>Review stays connected to implementation.</h2><p>Olena applies the risk-based QA approach, defines or refines acceptance criteria, reviews layout, scale, fonts, responsive states, visual hierarchy, and the end-user journey, then coordinates changes and retest with engineering.</p></div>
        <div class="quality-orbit" data-reveal aria-label="Playable quality concerns"><span>Journey</span><span>Responsive</span><span>Evidence</span><span>Variants</span><strong>Decision</strong></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="service-crosslink section-shell" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">Defined engagement</p><div><h2>Need a bounded platform-readiness package?</h2><a class="text-link" href="/playable-ads/release-quality-platform-readiness/">See the package structure <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
    <section class="callout section-shell section-pad" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">Bring the current build</p><h2>What decision is the team preparing to make?</h2><p>Share the playable, specification, variants, target environments, known issues, and deadline. We will identify the useful review boundary.</p><button class="button" type="button" data-contact-open>Discuss a review</button></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
